* Stochastic thinking\n(MIT 6.0002, lecture 4)
** Determinism debate
*** Newtonian mechanics: every effect has a cause
*** Copenhagen doctrine: causal nondeterminism
*** Predictive nondeterminism: we lack the knowledge
*** Hidden coins: answer fixed, still unknown
** Stochastic processes
*** Next state = previous states + random element
*** Underdetermined vs stochastic specification
*** random.choice: uniform draw
** Probability by counting
*** Favourable / possible outcomes
*** 11111 in 5 rolls: 1/7776
*** Complement: P(A) = 1 - P(not A)
*** Product rule needs independence
*** Patriots vs Broncos: 22/64 becomes ~1
** Simulation
*** Outer loop of trials, inner trial, count, divide
*** Sample vs actual probability
*** Rare events need many trials
*** 1000 trials -> 0.0, 10^6 trials -> 0.000128
** Birthday problem
*** Pigeonhole: 367 people -> 1
*** Closed form for two sharing
*** Three sharing: 0.644 at N = 100
*** Non-uniform dates: 0.749, code change only
** Pseudo-random numbers
*** Deterministic generator + seed
*** random.seed(0) for reproducible runs
*** Debug with several seeds
*** Not for secrets: use secrets / os.urandom
left side
** Models
*** Descriptive, not prescriptive
*** "All models are wrong, but some are useful"
*** Successive refinement, what-if questions
